{"title": "Sectional Mock #99 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>Sankar gives a note book free on purchased of thirteen note book and also, he offers 2% discount. Sankar marked at what percentage above the cost price of the note book so that he gains 40% profit on whole transactions?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2352; &#2340;&#2375;&#2352;&#2361; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2379;&#2335; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2350;&#2369;&#2347;&#2381;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2361;&#2368; &#2357;&#2361; 2% &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2349;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2375; &#2354;&#2375;&#2344;&#2342;&#2375;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; 40% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2344;&#2379;&#2335; &#2348;&#2369;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["53.84%", "61.89%", "45.29%", "38.72%"], "options_hi": ["53.84%", "61.89%", "45.29%", "38.72%"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let marked price of 13 note book = Rs. 100x</p><p>SP of {(13 + 1) = } 14 articles = 100x * 98/100 = Rs. 98x</p><p>SP of each article = 98x/14 = Rs. 7x</p><p>Cost price of each article = 7x * 100/140 = Rs. 5x</p><p>So, cost price of 13 articles = Rs. 65x</p><p>So, marked up % = (100x  -  65x)/65x * 100 = 53.84%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let marked price of 13 note book = Rs. 100x</p><p>SP of {(13 + 1) = } 14 articles = 100x * 98/100 = Rs. 98x</p><p>SP of each article = 98x/14 = Rs. 7x</p><p>Cost price of each article = 7x * 100/140 = Rs. 5x</p><p>So, cost price of 13 articles = Rs. 65x</p><p>So, marked up % = (100x  -  65x)/65x * 100 = 53.84%</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a sum of Rs. (P-1000), at 15% per annum compounded annually for two years, is amounted to Rs. (P+1580), then what is the value of P?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; (P-1000) &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367;, 15% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2361; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; (P+1580) &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; P &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8000", "9000", "10080", "9500"], "options_hi": ["8000", "9000", "10080", "9500"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>P + 1580 = (P  -  1000)(1 + 15/100)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; P + 1580 = (P  -  1000) * 529/400</p><p>=&gt; 400P + 632000 = 529P  -  529000</p><p>=&gt; 129P = 1161000</p><p>=&gt; P = 9000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>P + 1580 = (P  -  1000)(1 + 15/100)<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; P + 1580 = (P  -  1000) * 529/400</p><p>=&gt; 400P + 632000 = 529P  -  529000</p><p>=&gt; 129P = 1161000</p><p>=&gt; P = 9000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following fractions is nearest to 23/31?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>0.<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">11", "options_en": ["27/39", "15/28", "22/29", "17/22"], "options_hi": ["0.<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">88", "0.<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">87", "0.<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">8", "0.8<span style=\"text-decoration:overline\">8"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>23/31 = 0.74</p><p>(a) 27/39 = 0.69</p><p>(b) 15/28 = 0.53</p><p>(c) 22/29 = 0.758 [Nearest]</p><p>(d) 17/22 = 0.77</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>23/31 = 0.74</p><p>(a) 27/39 = 0.69</p><p>(b) 15/28 = 0.53</p><p>(c) 22/29 = 0.758 [Nearest]</p><p>(d) 17/22 = 0.77</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A boat can travel 48 km downstream in 3 hours and the same distance upstream in 6 hours. Find the speed of the boat in still water.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; 48 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2370;&#2354; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2352; &#2332;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10 kmph", "8 kmph", "12 kmph", "9 kmph"], "options_hi": ["10 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "8 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "9 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Downstream speed = 48/3 = 16 kmph</p><p>Upstream speed = 48/6 = 8 kmph</p><p>Speed of the boat in still water = (1/2) (Downstream speed + upstream speed) = 12 kmph</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Downstream speed = 48/3 = 16 kmph</p><p>Upstream speed = 48/6 = 8 kmph</p><p>Speed of the boat in still water = (1/2) (Downstream speed + upstream speed) = 12 kmph</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>(2x + 3y)/(3x  -  2y) = 3/4, then what is the value of (x<sup>2</sup> + 2y<sup>2</sup>)/(x<sup>2</sup>  -  4y<sup>2</sup>)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>(2x + 3y)/(3x - 2y) = 3/4 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (x<sup>2</sup> + 2y<sup>2</sup>)/(x<sup>2</sup> - 4y<sup>2</sup>) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["129/120", "177/160", "163/160", "172/161"], "options_hi": ["129/120", "177/160", "163/160", "172/161"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>(2x + 3y)/(3x  -  2y) = 3/4</p><p>=&gt; 8x + 12y = 9x  -  6y</p><p>=&gt; 18y = x</p><p>=&gt; x/y = 18/1</p><p>=&gt; x = 18k and y = k</p><p>Hence, (x<sup>2</sup> + 2y<sup>2</sup>)/(3x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup>) = ((18k)<sup>2</sup> + 2(k)<sup>2</sup>)/((18k)<sup>2</sup>  -  4(k)<sup>2</sup>) = (324k<sup>2</sup> + 2k<sup>2</sup>)/(324k<sup>2</sup>  -  4k<sup>2</sup>) = 326/320 = 163/160</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(2x + 3y)/(3x  -  2y) = 3/4</p><p>=&gt; 8x + 12y = 9x  -  6y</p><p>=&gt; 18y = x</p><p>=&gt; x/y = 18/1</p><p>=&gt; x = 18k and y = k</p><p>Hence, (x<sup>2</sup> + 2y<sup>2</sup>)/(3x<sup>2</sup>  -  y<sup>2</sup>) = ((18k)<sup>2</sup> + 2(k)<sup>2</sup>)/((18k)<sup>2</sup>  -  4(k)<sup>2</sup>) = (324k<sup>2</sup> + 2k<sup>2</sup>)/(324k<sup>2</sup>  -  4k<sup>2</sup>) = 326/320 = 163/160</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of a table top in the shape of an equilateral triangle is 9&radic;3 cm<sup>2</sup>. What is the length (in cm) of each side of the table top?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 9&radic;3 cm<sup>2 </sup>&#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2375;&#2332; &#2325;&#2375; &#2358;&#2368;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; (cm &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["6", "2", "4", "3"], "options_hi": ["6", "2", "4", "3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let side of table top = 'a' cm</p><p>Area of table top = <img width=83 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19946/image060.png\"></p><p>a = 6</p><p>Length of each side = 6 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let side of table top = 'a' cm</p><p>Area of table top = <img width=83 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p19946/image060.png\"></p><p>a = 6</p><p>Length of each side = 6 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>There are two numbers a and b such that a&gt;b. a exceeds b by one-third of b. If a is divided by b, quotient is 1 and remainder is 250. Find the smaller number.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; a &#2324;&#2352; b &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; a&gt;b &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; a, b &#2360;&#2375; b &#2325;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325;-&#2340;&#2367;&#2361;&#2366;&#2312; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; a &#2325;&#2379; b &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2347;&#2354; 1 &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2347;&#2354; 250 &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["250", "625", "750", "1000"], "options_hi": ["250", "625", "750", "1000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Since, a &gt; b</p><p>a  -  b = b/3</p><p>a = b + b/3= 4b/3, and</p><p>a = 1*b + 250</p><p>Hence, b + 25= 4b/3</p><p>3b + 750 = 4b</p><p>b = 750 (smaller number).</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since, a &gt; b</p><p>a  -  b = b/3</p><p>a = b + b/3= 4b/3, and</p><p>a = 1*b + 250</p><p>Hence, b + 25= 4b/3</p><p>3b + 750 = 4b</p><p>b = 750 (smaller number).</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>If Y = 4X + 3, then what is the value (64X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> + 36XY)? </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; Y = 4X + 3, &#2340;&#2379; (64X<sup>3</sup> - Y<sup>3</sup> + 36XY) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["27", "-27", "-64", "64"], "options_hi": ["27", "-27", "-64", "64"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>4X  -  Y = -3 </p><p>=&gt; (4X  -  Y)<sup>3</sup> = -3<sup>3</sup></p><p>=&gt; 64X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>  -  3 * 4XY (4X  -  Y) = -27 </p><p>=&gt; 64X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> + 36XY = -27</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>4X  -  Y = -3 </p><p>=&gt; (4X  -  Y)<sup>3</sup> = -3<sup>3</sup></p><p>=&gt; 64X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>  -  3 * 4XY (4X  -  Y) = -27 </p><p>=&gt; 64X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> + 36XY = -27</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Shweta and Sheela are partners in a traveling business. Shweta invests Rs. 75000 for 8 months and Sheela invests Rs. 80000 for 10 months. Out of total profit of Rs. 63140, what will be the share of profit of Shweta?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2357;&#2354;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2368;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 75000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2368;&#2354;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; 10 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 80000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; 63140 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349;&#2366;&#2306;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs. 24040", "Rs. 21080", "Rs. 27030", "Rs. 27060"], "options_hi": ["24040 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "21080 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "27030 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "27060 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Ratio of investment of Shweta and Sheela = (75000 * 8): (80000 * 10) = 3: 4</p><p>Hence, share of profit of Shweta = 3/7 * 63140 = Rs. 27060</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Ratio of investment of Shweta and Sheela = (75000 * 8): (80000 * 10) = 3: 4</p><p>Hence, share of profit of Shweta = 3/7 * 63140 = Rs. 27060</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The perimeter of a rectangular garden is 48 m. If the length is 6 m more than the breadth, the area (in m<sup>2</sup>) of the garden is:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2343;&#2367; 48 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2327;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (&#2350;&#2368;<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:", "options_en": ["135", "96", "84", "112"], "options_hi": ["135", "96", "84", "112"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let Breadth be B.</p><p>Then, Length L = B + 6</p><p>Perimeter = 2(L + B)</p><p>48 = 2(B + 6 + B)</p><p>48 = 2(2B + 6)</p><p>48 = 4B + 12</p><p>=&gt; 4B = 48 - 12</p><p>=&gt; 4B = 36</p><p>=&gt; B = 36 / 4</p><p>=&gt; B = 9</p><p>Length L = B + 6</p><p>=&gt; 9 + 6 = 15</p><p>Area = L  X  B</p><p>=&gt; 15  X  9 = 135 m<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Breadth be B.</p><p>Then, Length L = B + 6</p><p>Perimeter = 2(L + B)</p><p>48 = 2(B + 6 + B)</p><p>48 = 2(2B + 6)</p><p>48 = 4B + 12</p><p>=&gt; 4B = 48 - 12</p><p>=&gt; 4B = 36</p><p>=&gt; B = 36 / 4</p><p>=&gt; B = 9</p><p>Length L = B + 6</p><p>=&gt; 9 + 6 = 15</p><p>Area = L  X  B</p><p>=&gt; 15  X  9 = 135 m<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>The table given below shows the number of three types of vehicles sold by a company in three different months and the pie chart shows the unsold vehicles in those months together.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Month</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Scooters</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Bikes</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Bicycle</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">July</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">200</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">500</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">123</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">August</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">135</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">211</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">422</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">September</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">432</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">330</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">260</td></tr></table><p><img width=292 height=250 id=\"Chart 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image017.png\"></p><p>If the number of unsold vehicles in all three months together are 350, then find the number of bicycles manufactured in all three months together.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2309;&#2354;&#2327;-&#2309;&#2354;&#2327; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2313;&#2344; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2344; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2366;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;&#2367;&#2354;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2332;&#2369;&#2354;&#2366;&#2312;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">200</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">500</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">123</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2309;&#2327;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">135</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">211</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">422</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2367;&#2340;&#2306;&#2348;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">432</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">330</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">260</td></tr></table><p><img width=292 height=250 id=\"Chart 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27549/image017.png\"></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2348;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 350 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2360;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["960", "875", "925", "840"], "options_hi": ["960", "875", "925", "840"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Number of unsold vehicles in all three months together = 350</p><p>Number of unsold bicycles in all three months together = 20% of 350 = 70</p><p>Number of bicycles manufactured in all three months together = 70 + (123 + 422 + 260) = 875</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of unsold vehicles in all three months together = 350</p><p>Number of unsold bicycles in all three months together = 20% of 350 = 70</p><p>Number of bicycles manufactured in all three months together = 70 + (123 + 422 + 260) = 875</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is volume of the frustum of the cone, if the radius of the upper base of the frustum of the cone and height of the frustum of the cone are 20 cm and 10.5 cm respectively, and the radius of the lower base is 10 cm?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2314;&#2346;&#2352;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2325; &#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 20 cm &#2324;&#2352; 10.5 cm &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2367;&#2330;&#2354;&#2375; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 10 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369; &#2325;&#2375; &#2331;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2351;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["7500 cm<sup>3</sup>", "6600 cm<sup>3</sup>", "7700 cm<sup>3</sup>", "7200 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["7500 cm<sup>3</sup>", "6600 cm<sup>3</sup>", "7700 cm<sup>3</sup>", "7200 cm<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the frustum of the cone = 1/3 * 22/7 * H * (R<sup>2</sup> + Rr + r<sup>2</sup>) = 1/3 * 22/7 * 10.5 * (400 + 200 + 100) = 7700 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the frustum of the cone = 1/3 * 22/7 * H * (R<sup>2</sup> + Rr + r<sup>2</sup>) = 1/3 * 22/7 * 10.5 * (400 + 200 + 100) = 7700 cm<sup>3</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Seema walks around a circular field at the rate of 3 rounds per hour, while Priya runs around it at the rate of 8 rounds per hour. They start in the same direction from the same point at 11:54 PM. They shall first cross each other at:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2360;&#2368;&#2350;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2376;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; 3 &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2323;&#2352; 8 &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; 11:54 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2342;&#2367;&#2358;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2357;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2375;:", "options_en": ["12:06 p.m.", "12:00 a.m.", "12:06 a.m.", "11:59 p.m."], "options_hi": ["12:06 p.m.", "12:00 a.m.", "12:06 a.m.", "11:59 p.m."], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Relative Speed = 8  -  3 = 5 rounds/hour</p><p>Time taken to first cross each other = 1/5 hours or 12 minutes</p><p>They start at 11:54 p.m.</p><p>=&gt; 11:54 p.m. + 12 minutes = 12:06 a.m.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Relative Speed = 8  -  3 = 5 rounds/hour</p><p>Time taken to first cross each other = 1/5 hours or 12 minutes</p><p>They start at 11:54 p.m.</p><p>=&gt; 11:54 p.m. + 12 minutes = 12:06 a.m.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p> A man purchases a motor bike for a certain price and promise to pay the price in two equal annual Instalments of Rs.13230 at the rate of 5% per annum compounded annually. Find the cost price of motor bike. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 5% &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 13230 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2311;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.24600", "Rs.17640", "Rs.25200", "Rs.22050"], "options_hi": ["24600 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "17640 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "25200 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "22050 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/d11a51460064e5d9e08878933129f5d7.png\" /> </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> <img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/d11a51460064e5d9e08878933129f5d7.png\" /> </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>A person takes a loan of Rs. 260 at 5% simple interest .He returns Rs. 150 at the end of one year. In order to clear his dues at the end of 2 year, he would pay-</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; 5% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 260 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2315;&#2339; &#2354;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 150 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2354;&#2380;&#2335;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2325;&#2366;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["123.15 Rs.", "122.23 Rs.", "132.45 Rs.", "129.15 R"], "options_hi": ["123.15 &#2352;&#2369;.", "122.23 &#2352;&#2369;.", "132.45 &#2352;&#2369;.", "129.15 &#2352;&#2369;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Amount to be paid in first year= 260 + [(260  X 5  X 1)/100] = 260 + 13= 273</p><p>Amount left as principal for second year = 273  -  150= 123</p><p>So, Amount paid in second year= 123 + [(123  X 5  X 1)]/100 =123 + 6.15 = 129.15</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Amount to be paid in first year= 260 + [(260  X 5  X 1)/100] = 260 + 13= 273</p><p>Amount left as principal for second year = 273  -  150= 123</p><p>So, Amount paid in second year= 123 + [(123  X 5  X 1)]/100 =123 + 6.15 = 129.15</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the single discount equivalent to a series discount of 30%, 20% and 15%</p>", "q_hi": "<p>30%, 20% &#2324;&#2352; 15% &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2371;&#2306;&#2326;&#2354;&#2366; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2319;&#2325;&#2354; &#2331;&#2370;&#2335; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;</p>", "options_en": ["51.4%", "52.4%", "62.4%", "72.4%"], "options_hi": ["51.4%", "52.4%", "62.4%", "72.4%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let the marked price = Rs 100</p><p>Then, Net SP = 70% of 80% of 85% of Rs 100</p><p>= 0.7 * 0.8 * 0.85 * 100</p><p>= Rs 47.6</p><p>Therefore, required discount = 100  -  47.6</p><p>= 52.4 %</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the marked price = Rs 100</p><p>Then, Net SP = 70% of 80% of 85% of Rs 100</p><p>= 0.7 * 0.8 * 0.85 * 100</p><p>= Rs 47.6</p><p>Therefore, required discount = 100  -  47.6</p><p>= 52.4 %</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cylinder of height 8 cm and radius 6 cm is melted and converted into 3 cones of the same radius and height that of cylinder. Determine the total curved surface area of cones.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>8 cm &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2324;&#2352; 6 cm &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2328;&#2354;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2348;&#2375;&#2354;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; 3 &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2310;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2306;&#2325;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2357;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["180 &#960; cm2", "60 &#960; cm2", "144 &#960; cm2", "120 &#960; cm2"], "options_hi": ["180 &#960; cm2", "60 &#960; cm2", "144 &#960; cm2", "120 &#960; cm2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Radius of cone = Radius of cylinder = r = 6 cm</p><p>Height of cone = Height of cylinder = h = 8 cm</p><p>Lateral height of cone = &radic;(8<sup>2</sup> + 6<sup>2</sup>) = l = 10 cm</p><p>Curved surface area of one cone = &#960;rl = &#960; * 6 * 10 = 60&#960; cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Curved surface area of three such cones = 3 * 60&#960; = 180&#960; cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Radius of cone = Radius of cylinder = r = 6 cm</p><p>Height of cone = Height of cylinder = h = 8 cm</p><p>Lateral height of cone = &radic;(8<sup>2</sup> + 6<sup>2</sup>) = l = 10 cm</p><p>Curved surface area of one cone = &#960;rl = &#960; * 6 * 10 = 60&#960; cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>Curved surface area of three such cones = 3 * 60&#960; = 180&#960; cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 2X  -  Y = 6, and 4X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = 60, then find the value of 8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 2X - Y = 6 &#2324;&#2352; 4X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup> = 60 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 8X<sup>3</sup> - Y<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["432", "0", "-185", "180"], "options_hi": ["432", "0", "-185", "180"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Given,</p><p>2X  -  Y = 6</p><p>Square both sides,</p><p>4X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>  -  4XY = 36</p><p>60  -  4XY = 36</p><p>4XY = 60  -  36</p><p>4XY = 24</p><p>XY = 6</p><p>Given,</p><p>2X  -  Y = 6</p><p>Cube both sides,</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>  -  3* 2X * Y * (2X  -  Y) = 216</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>  -  6 * 6 * 6 = 216</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = 216 + 216</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = 432</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given,</p><p>2X  -  Y = 6</p><p>Square both sides,</p><p>4X<sup>2</sup> + Y<sup>2</sup>  -  4XY = 36</p><p>60  -  4XY = 36</p><p>4XY = 60  -  36</p><p>4XY = 24</p><p>XY = 6</p><p>Given,</p><p>2X  -  Y = 6</p><p>Cube both sides,</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>  -  3* 2X * Y * (2X  -  Y) = 216</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup>  -  6 * 6 * 6 = 216</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = 216 + 216</p><p>8X<sup>3</sup>  -  Y<sup>3</sup> = 432</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>A freight train travels at 36 km/h. A passenger train, 30 km/h faster than the freight train, overtakes it and crosses completely in 18 seconds. If the length of the passenger train is 120 m, find the length of the freight train (in m).</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; 36 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354; &#2352;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; 30 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2375; &#2323;&#2357;&#2352;&#2335;&#2375;&#2325; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; 18 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2352;&#2361; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2368; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 120 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2366;&#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; (&#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["25", "20", "30", "40"], "options_hi": ["25", "20", "30", "40"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let L = length of freight train in meters</p><p>Speed of freight train = 36 km/h = 36  X  (5/18) = 10 m/s</p><p>Speed of passenger train = 36 + 30 = 66 km/h = 66  X  (5/18) = 55/3 m/s</p><p>Relative speed (same direction) = (55/3) &#8722; 10 = 25/3 m/s</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(120 + L) / (25/3) = 18</p><p>=&gt; (120 + L) = 18  X  (25/3) = 150</p><p>=&gt; L = 150 &#8722; 120 = 30</p><p>Thus, the length of the freight train is 30 m.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let L = length of freight train in meters</p><p>Speed of freight train = 36 km/h = 36  X  (5/18) = 10 m/s</p><p>Speed of passenger train = 36 + 30 = 66 km/h = 66  X  (5/18) = 55/3 m/s</p><p>Relative speed (same direction) = (55/3) &#8722; 10 = 25/3 m/s</p><p>According to question,</p><p>(120 + L) / (25/3) = 18</p><p>=&gt; (120 + L) = 18  X  (25/3) = 150</p><p>=&gt; L = 150 &#8722; 120 = 30</p><p>Thus, the length of the freight train is 30 m.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>7<sup>15</sup> + 7<sup>16</sup> + 7<sup>17</sup> is divisible by which of the following given numbers?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>7<sup>15</sup> + 7<sup>16</sup> + 7<sup>17</sup> &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["3", "5", "2", "4"], "options_hi": ["3", "5", "2", "4"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Take 7<sup>15</sup> common from the expression:</p><p>7<sup>15</sup>+7<sup>16</sup>+7<sup>17</sup>=7<sup>15</sup>(1+7+7<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>1+7+7<sup>2</sup>=1+7+49=57</p><p>thus, the expression becomes:</p><p>7<sup>15</sup> X 57</p><p>Now, factor 57:</p><p>57=3 X 19</p><p>So it is divisible by 3,7 and 19</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Take 7<sup>15</sup> common from the expression:</p><p>7<sup>15</sup>+7<sup>16</sup>+7<sup>17</sup>=7<sup>15</sup>(1+7+7<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>1+7+7<sup>2</sup>=1+7+49=57</p><p>thus, the expression becomes:</p><p>7<sup>15</sup> X 57</p><p>Now, factor 57:</p><p>57=3 X 19</p><p>So it is divisible by 3,7 and 19</p><p>Option (a) is the correct answer.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>The area of a triangle is 480 cm<sup>2</sup> and the ratio of its sides is 10:24:26. What is the perimeter of the triangle?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 480 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 10:24:26 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["120 cm", "30 cm", "150 cm", "60 cm"], "options_hi": ["120 cm", "30 cm", "150 cm", "60 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let sides are 10x cm, 24x cm, and 26x cm, respectively.</p><p>Area = 480 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 1/2 * 10x * 24x = 480</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> = 480 * 2/(240) = 4</p><p>=&gt; x = 2</p><p>So, perimeter of the triangle = 2(10 + 24 + 26) = 120 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let sides are 10x cm, 24x cm, and 26x cm, respectively.</p><p>Area = 480 cm<sup>2</sup></p><p>=&gt; 1/2 * 10x * 24x = 480</p><p>=&gt; x<sup>2</sup> = 480 * 2/(240) = 4</p><p>=&gt; x = 2</p><p>So, perimeter of the triangle = 2(10 + 24 + 26) = 120 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Anil sells sugar at cost price but uses false weights and thus makes 20% profit. How many grams of sugar does he give in 1 kilogram?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2367;&#2354; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2327;&#2340; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; 20% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; 1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["833.23", "833.13", "833.33", "823.33"], "options_hi": ["833.23", "833.13", "833.33", "823.33"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let CP per kg = C, he gives w grams instead of 1000 grams</p><p>Cost of w grams = (w / 1000) * C</p><p>SP = C (sells at CP), Profit = 20%</p><p>Profit = (C - (w/1000)C) / ((w/1000)C) = 0.2</p><p>(1 - w/1000) / (w/1000) = 0.2</p><p>1000 - w = 0.2w</p><p>1000 = 1.2w</p><p>w = 1000 / 1.2 = <b>833.33</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let CP per kg = C, he gives w grams instead of 1000 grams</p><p>Cost of w grams = (w / 1000) * C</p><p>SP = C (sells at CP), Profit = 20%</p><p>Profit = (C - (w/1000)C) / ((w/1000)C) = 0.2</p><p>(1 - w/1000) / (w/1000) = 0.2</p><p>1000 - w = 0.2w</p><p>1000 = 1.2w</p><p>w = 1000 / 1.2 = <b>833.33</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If [(a/x) + (b/y)] = 1 and [(x/a) + (y/b)] = -4/3, then what is the value of [(a/x)<sup>3</sup> + (b/y)<sup>3</sup>]?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; [(a/x) + (b/y)] = 1 &#2324;&#2352; [(x/a) + (y/b)] = -4/3, &#2340;&#2379; [(a/x)<sup>3</sup> + (b/y)<sup>3</sup>] &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["(9/4)", "(13/4)", "(17/4)", "(13/7)"], "options_hi": ["(9/4)", "(13/4)", "(17/4)", "(13/7)"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>[(a/x) + (b/y)] = 1</p><p>Let (a/x) = p and (b/y) = q</p><p>(p + q) = 1 ......... (1)</p><p>[(x/a) + (y/b)] = -4/3</p><p>(1/p) + (1/q) = -4/3</p><p>(q + p)pq = -4/3</p><p>1/pq = -4/3</p><p>pq = -3/4 ........ (2)</p><p>= [(a/x)<sup>3</sup> + (b/y)<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>= [p<sup>3</sup> + q<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>= (p + q)<sup>3</sup>  -  3pq(p + q)</p><p>From equations (1) and (2)-</p><p>= 1<sup>3</sup>  -  3 * (-3/4) * (1)</p><p>= 1 + (9/4)</p><p>= (13/4)</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>[(a/x) + (b/y)] = 1</p><p>Let (a/x) = p and (b/y) = q</p><p>(p + q) = 1 ......... (1)</p><p>[(x/a) + (y/b)] = -4/3</p><p>(1/p) + (1/q) = -4/3</p><p>(q + p)pq = -4/3</p><p>1/pq = -4/3</p><p>pq = -3/4 ........ (2)</p><p>= [(a/x)<sup>3</sup> + (b/y)<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>= [p<sup>3</sup> + q<sup>3</sup>]</p><p>= (p + q)<sup>3</sup>  -  3pq(p + q)</p><p>From equations (1) and (2)-</p><p>= 1<sup>3</sup>  -  3 * (-3/4) * (1)</p><p>= 1 + (9/4)</p><p>= (13/4)</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a 975-meter underground tunnel sprint between two futuristic robots, Robo-X races at a speed of 23.4 km/h. Out of courtesy, Robo-X gives Robo-Y a 50-meter head start-but still finishes 35 seconds ahead. What is Robo-Y's running speed?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2349;&#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2368; &#2352;&#2379;&#2348;&#2379;&#2335;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; 975 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2349;&#2370;&#2350;&#2367;&#2327;&#2340; &#2360;&#2369;&#2352;&#2306;&#2327; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2306;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2352;&#2379;&#2348;&#2379;-&#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; 23.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2358;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2335;&#2366;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375;, &#2352;&#2379;&#2348;&#2379;-&#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2352;&#2379;&#2348;&#2379;-&#2357;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2379; 50 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2348;&#2338;&#2364;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;-&#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2347;&#2367;&#2352; &#2349;&#2368; 35 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2310;&#2327;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2352;&#2379;&#2348;&#2379;-&#2357;&#2366;&#2312; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["27 km/h", "12 km/h", "16 km/h", "18 km/h"], "options_hi": ["27 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "16 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "18 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18] </b></p><p>23.4 km/h = 6.5 m/s</p><p>Time taken by X to cover 975 m = 975/6.5 = 150 seconds </p><p>Distance covered by Y = 975  -  50 = 925 m</p><p>Time taken by Y to cover 925 m = 150 + 35 = 185 seconds </p><p>Hence, the speed of Y = 925/185 = 5 m/s = 5 * 18/5 = 18 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><b>[To convert km/h in m/s, multiply with 5/18] </b></p><p>23.4 km/h = 6.5 m/s</p><p>Time taken by X to cover 975 m = 975/6.5 = 150 seconds </p><p>Distance covered by Y = 975  -  50 = 925 m</p><p>Time taken by Y to cover 925 m = 150 + 35 = 185 seconds </p><p>Hence, the speed of Y = 925/185 = 5 m/s = 5 * 18/5 = 18 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>There were two candidates A and B. During an election, 12% of voters in the voter list did not vote, and 360 voters cast blank ballot papers. If the winner A was supported by 52% of all voters in the list and obtained 1384 more votes than B, then find the total number of voters in the voter list. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2313;&#2350;&#2381;&#2350;&#2368;&#2342;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366;&#2357; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;, &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 12% &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2344; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2324;&#2352; 360 &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2326;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2350;&#2340;&#2346;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; A &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; 52% &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2341;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; B &#2360;&#2375; 1384 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2379;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2340;&#2342;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["8000", "7500", "9500", "6400"], "options_hi": ["8000", "7500", "9500", "6400"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the total number of voters in the voter list be '100X'</p><p>The total number of voters who did not vote = 100X * 12/100 = 12X</p><p>The total number of voters who supported A = 100X * 52/100 = 52X</p><p>The total number of voters who supported B = 52X  -  1384</p><p>A/Q</p><p>52X + 52X  -  1384 + 360 = 100X  -  12X</p><p>16X = 1024</p><p>X = 64</p><p>Hence, the required voters = 64 * 100 = 6400</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the total number of voters in the voter list be '100X'</p><p>The total number of voters who did not vote = 100X * 12/100 = 12X</p><p>The total number of voters who supported A = 100X * 52/100 = 52X</p><p>The total number of voters who supported B = 52X  -  1384</p><p>A/Q</p><p>52X + 52X  -  1384 + 360 = 100X  -  12X</p><p>16X = 1024</p><p>X = 64</p><p>Hence, the required voters = 64 * 100 = 6400</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}]}